      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, with a nuance. The suppression marker is now the queue\u0027s own \"requested\" state (in flight or pending), so there is no separate set to leak. The facade settles it after its check for every isOver status via attachmentTransferOver(): TRANSFER_FINISHED and TRANSFER_ERROR (invalid_pathname/unsupported, where the daemon drops the request) end it; TRANSFER_UNJOINABLE_PEER/TRANSFER_TIMEOUT_EXPIRED (closed_by_host/peer, unjoinable, timeout, where the daemon keeps the request and retries) move it to pending, so the later retry and its FINISHED event stay silent for this old message. Events that do not reach the facade are settled by AccountService itself (dispatchDataTransferEvent reports whether it propagated). A user cancel (cancelDataTransfer) and the removal of the conversation or account drop the entry.",
